  "summary": "Pediatric behavioral healthcare continues to emerge as a critical gap in the health system, with coverage today on both how technology might bridge access problems and the specific barriers preventing care delivery. In oncology and obesity treatment, several major developments point to a reshaping of available options: AstraZeneca's oral GLP-1 candidate shows promise as an alternative to injectables, while J&J's billion-dollar acquisition of Firefly Bio signals intensifying competition in the KRAS inhibitor space, and combination therapies from Tango and Revolution are yielding strong early results in pancreatic cancer. Across healthcare organizations, critical infrastructure challenges are taking priority, including data governance obstacles that must be resolved before AI implementations can succeed, supply chain resilience that needs elevation to corporate strategy level, and EHR transitions at major facilities like VA hospitals and Taipei Veterans General. Remote patient monitoring is expanding under 2026 policy changes, though operational complexity is increasing, while emerging innovations like Google's smartphone-based heart rate monitoring and Oura's new AI ring reflect growing consumer-facing health tracking capabilities.",
